;; rsi's divergences from rustc 1.99.1 on ci (doc/rust/EVAL.md §9; doc/rust/RUST-EVAL-SURVEY.md, "As built: RE4 (write-ahead)"):
;; the classes every program of bin/rsi check that does not pass falls into, each with why and where it was decided, in
;; test/goi/divergences.edn's format. A program's class is the first whose :match finds its result and reason ("RESULT REASON",
;; as test/rust/check-linux-amd64.edn writes them); :nondet (the judge's own runs differ) is a result, not a class. bin/rsi
;; divergences judges the recorded check against them. Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :process
  :title "processes (deferred: ci spawns none)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "std::process::Command spawns by musl's posix_spawn, a clone of a process (CLONE_VM | CLONE_VFORK, no CLONE_THREAD): ci's back end runs one process, its __clone (since RE6 a thread's, go/arbace/ci/thread.ae) refuses it (C's class, EVAL.md §6's process set)"
  :decided "RES7 (a), RES22 (a); C's §6.5"
  :match [#"of a process: ci runs one process" #"undefined function __clone at 0x0 in posix_spawn" #"undefined function (fork|execve?|__clone) .*Command"]}
 {:id :threads
  :title "threads (what ci's scheduler does not run)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "since RE6 ci runs threads (go/arbace/crt/sched.ae, go/arbace/ci/thread.ae: goroutines, one running at a time, the baton passed at futex waits, sleeps, yields, exits and every 20,000 calls; thread-local objects swapped); a thread start or wait it does not take (a clone of another kind, a deadlock every thread waits in) is here; before RE6, every spawn (RES7 (a) left threads out of v1)"
  :decided "RES7 (a); C's §6.5"
  :match [#"undefined function __clone" #"failed to spawn thread" #"deadlock: every thread waits"]}
 {:id :speed
  :title "speed: programs beyond the check's budget"
  :kind :design
  :why "an interpreter of nodes is 10 to 100 times slower than rustc's -O0 code (C's, C++'s and goi's class of the same name)"
  :decided "C's CS107 (a); survey §14"
  :match [#"^fail differ status timeout"]}
 {:id :not-lowered
  :title "a stub of std reached (f16)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "std's functions the lowering does not take (core's f16) are stubs that abort with their name (EVAL.md §8); f16 and f128 at RE5"
  :decided "RES24 (a)"
  :match [#"rsi: not lowered"]}
 {:id :env
  :title "the environment: ci starts a program with an empty one (a ci design, C's)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "go/arbace/ci's RunMain gave __libc_start_main an empty envp (its doc: \"an empty environment\"), so a program's exec-env (compiletest's, run-program's env -i NAME=VALUE) was not seen: std::env::var gave NotPresent where the original reads the value; since RE6 (RES29 (a)) rsi's runs give cirun and the compiled programs --env, the runner's environment, so a program here is one whose environment still differs"
  :decided "RE4 (this record); RES29 proposes ci's envp from the runner's environment"
  :match [#"^fail differ .*\(exec-env\)$" #"^fail known env: "]}
 {:id :ci-param-width
  :title "ci does not narrow a parameter to its type on entry (a ci gap, C's to fix)"
  :kind :gap
  :why "a callee whose parameter is narrower than the caller's argument (the lowering's unsigned char for Rust's i8, called into C's int8_t: rust_test_helpers' rust_int8_to_int32) reads the caller's whole value on ci (255 where gcc's callee gives -1: bin/ci run of a cast call, RE4); the x86-64 ABI leaves the callee to narrow"
  :decided "RE4 (this record); reported to C's crop"
  :match [#"^fail known ci-param-width: "]}
 {:id :c-variadic
  :title "C-variadic Rust functions (va_start without a named parameter)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "a Rust `extern \"C\" fn f(...)` defined in Rust (c_variadic) lowers to va_start without a named parameter, which C23 allows and the lowering refuses (RE2's lower class c-variadic)"
  :decided "RE2's divergences-lower.edn c-variadic"
  :match [#"^lower-refused va: "]}
 {:id :lto
  :title "LTO and many codegen units: the program's IR is not one unit"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "a test built with -C lto=thin or fat, or codegen units the wrapper's -C codegen-units=1 does not override, gives rustc's link more than one unit (RE2's lower class lto)"
  :decided "RE2's divergences-lower.edn lto"
  :match [#"^ir-refused cgu: "]}
]
